  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/agr1400.html",
  "prefLabel": "Agr 1407.07 Renewing Device Licenses",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Agr 1407.07 Renewing Device Licenses.\n\n(a) The division shall provide via mail, e-mail, or fax to each owner of a device license a “Renewal for Weighing and Measuring Device License Form” containing pre-printed information at least 60 days prior to the expiration of the licensee’s license.\n\n(b) Owners of licensed devices who have not received such a renewal application form shall notify the division by mail, telephone, e-mail or fax.\n\n(c) Device owners wishing to renew their device licenses shall:\n\n(1) Confirm or correct the information on the division generated renewal application form including verifying the following:\n\na. Device category;\n\nb. Make, model and serial number;\n\nc. Equipment location;\n\nd. Number of meters; and\n\ne. Certification date;\n\n(2) Prior to a license being issued, submit proof of certification, such as a placed in service report, with the renewal that the devices have been inspected and certified and display a current year or previous year certification stamp;\n\n(3) Return the signed renewal application form with any changes to the division; and\n\n(4) Pay the division's invoice within 30 days.\n\n(d) Upon receipt of (1)-(4) above, a license shall be issued and sent to the device owner or authorized agent.\n\nSource. #9639, eff 1-20-10; ss by #10976, eff 11-20-15; ss by #12424, eff 12-1-17 (See Revision Note #2 at chapter heading for Agr 1400)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/agr1400.html"
